{
  "_doc": "JSON paths read by collectors/graphql.py. A path is a list of dict keys (strings) and list indices (integers); \"*\" means every item of a list. Each field is a list of alternative paths tried in order: the first value that converts wins (integers, numeric strings, or display strings such as \"1,2 Tr\" for counts). Paths for story fields start at the Story node; both comet_sections-wrapped and direct content/feedback projections are supported. Duplicate Story nodes fill missing fields while retaining first-seen non-empty values. Paths for views, comments, shares, reactions and video_markers start at the counter block: the merge of every dict that the `feedback` paths reach (first-seen values win), so Reels counters split across feedback, fb_reel_react_button and media are all read. Deferred fragments that share the Story's node id are merged into the Story first. Page header paths (page_name, page_followers) start at a node whose __typename is in page_typenames: an old-style Page node, or the profile header renderer of new-style pages, whose `user` is the page itself (its `viewer` is the logged-in account and is never read). When Facebook changes its JSON, edit this file; no rebuild is needed. Synthetic fixtures: tests/fixtures/graphql_sample.txt and tests/fixtures/initial_page.html.",
